  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1035 PM CDT Sat May 9 2026\n\nAfter a cool and stormy Sunday, the rest of the week will be dry and \nhot. Upper ridging will build over the western CONUS and deamplify \nas it slowly pushes eastward through the week. Surface winds will \nshift to the south early Monday. Southerly surface flow and sunny \nskies will aide in warming temperatures to the low 80s across the \nregion Monday. Tuesday is when the real heat begins with as height \nand thickness increases due to the upper ridging as well as south to \nsouthwesterly surface flow, highs are expected to climb to the 90s. \nThese gross temperatures are expected everyday the rest of the week \nand possibly into the weekend. Subsidence from the upper ridging \nwill keep conditions dry. Moderate to breezy south to southwesterly \nwinds will also be possible each afternoon beginning Tuesday. With \nthe hot, windy, and dry conditions, elevated to critical fire danger \nwill be possible for much of next week.",
